# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored -- keep it that way, a
# beamtime directory gets shared, archived and sometimes published.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   1. the shell environment
#   2. this file
#   3. ~/.nrw
#   4. ~/.aure   (so a machine already set up for AuRE works here unchanged)
#
# `nrw doctor` reports which of these it actually read.
#
# Only needed for `nrw model new --from-notes`. Everything else in
# nr-workbench runs offline; if you have no endpoint, use
# `nrw model new --print-prompt` and hand that to the coding assistant
# already open on this project.

# --- one of these -----------------------------------------------------------

# The Claude Code CLI you already have. No key, no URL: AuRE runs `claude -p`
# as a subprocess and it uses whatever that binary is authenticated with --
# a subscription, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or your Bedrock / Vertex / Foundry setup.
# Costs more per call than a plain endpoint (~12k extra input tokens of Claude
# Code preamble) and adds ~1s of process startup; see AuRE's README.
# LLM_PROVIDER=claude_code
# AURE_CLAUDE_BIN=/path/to/claude   # only if it is not on PATH

# A hosted provider
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Google
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# LLM_API_KEY=...
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# A local or self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint (ollama, vLLM, LM Studio).
# No API key needed; the base URL is what marks it usable.
# LLM_PROVIDER=local
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1

# ALCF (Argonne). Uses a token from `alcf-auth`, not an API key.
# LLM_PROVIDER=alcf
# ALCF_CLUSTER=sophia

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# 0 is the default and the right choice here: filling in a spec from notes is
# extraction, not invention.
# LLM_TEMPERATURE=0
# LLM_TIMEOUT=120
